sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch05-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Contrary to what traditional science suggests, going from one to two or more dimensions produces some specific new effects but does not fundamentally change the overall behavior or the occurrence of complexity in simple programs.";
    dc:type "general-principle";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adding dimensions does not fundamentally change the occurrence of complexity";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 5, “Two Dimensions and Beyond”; section “Cellular Automata” (from p. 170), p. 170. Scope: simple programs (cellular automata, Turing machines, substitution systems) in one, two and three dimensions"
}
